09:01:48 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['University of Chicago\n1. The University of Chicago operates a significant number of research institutes and centers on campus, indicating a strong commitment to research and academic excellence.', "University of Chicago\n2. The Oriental Institute serves as both a museum and research center for Near Eastern studies, highlighting the university's focus on diverse and interdisciplinary research.", 'University of Chicago\n3. The presence of National Resource Centers, such as the Center for Middle Eastern Studies, suggests a dedicated focus on specific areas of study and scholarship.', "University of Chicago\n4. The partial management of Argonne National Laboratory and joint stake in Fermilab demonstrate the university's involvement in cutting-edge scientific research and collaboration with government institutions.", 'University of Chicago\n5. The collaboration with the Toyota Technological Institute at Chicago implies a focus on technology and engineering research, with potential implications for innovation and industry partnerships.', 'University of Chicago\n6. The announcement of affiliating the Marine Biological Laboratory in Woods Hole indicates a growing focus on marine research and environmental studies.', 'University of Chicago\n7. The presence of the National Opinion Research Center on campus suggests a focus on social sciences and data-driven research.', 'University of Chicago\n8. The diverse range of research institutions and centers affiliated with the university implies a broad and comprehensive approach to research and academic inquiry.', 'University of Chicago\n9. The involvement of faculty and students at the adjacent Toyota Technological Institute at Chicago in collaborative research activities suggests a strong emphasis on interdisciplinary cooperation and innovation.', 'University of Chicago\n10. The affiliation with the Marine Biological Laboratory in Woods Hole implies a growing interest in marine research and the potential for advancements in understanding and addressing environmental challenges.', "University of Chicago\nThe university operates 12 research institutes and 113 research centers on campus. Among these are the Oriental Institute—a museum and research center for Near Eastern studies owned and operated by the university—and a number of National Resource Centers, including the Center for Middle Eastern Studies. Chicago also operates or is affiliated with a number of research institutions apart from the university proper. The university partially manages Argonne National Laboratory, part of the United States Department of Energy's national laboratory system, and has a joint stake in Fermilab, a nearby particle physics laboratory, as well as a stake in the Apache Point Observatory in Sunspot, New Mexico. Faculty and students at the adjacent Toyota Technological Institute at Chicago collaborate with the university, In 2013, the university announced that it was affiliating the formerly independent Marine Biological Laboratory in Woods Hole, Mass. Although formally unrelated, the National Opinion Research Center is located on Chicago's campus."], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'University of Chicago', 'context': "The university operates 12 research institutes and 113 research centers on campus. Among these are the Oriental Institute—a museum and research center for Near Eastern studies owned and operated by the university—and a number of National Resource Centers, including the Center for Middle Eastern Studies. Chicago also operates or is affiliated with a number of research institutions apart from the university proper. The university partially manages Argonne National Laboratory, part of the United States Department of Energy's national laboratory system, and has a joint stake in Fermilab, a nearby particle physics laboratory, as well as a stake in the Apache Point Observatory in Sunspot, New Mexico. Faculty and students at the adjacent Toyota Technological Institute at Chicago collaborate with the university, In 2013, the university announced that it was affiliating the formerly independent Marine Biological Laboratory in Woods Hole, Mass. Although formally unrelated, the National Opinion Research Center is located on Chicago's campus.", 'question': 'Topic: University of Chicago\nHow many research institutes does the university run on campus?', 'answer': '12'}, {'title': 'University of Chicago', 'context': "The university operates 12 research institutes and 113 research centers on campus. Among these are the Oriental Institute—a museum and research center for Near Eastern studies owned and operated by the university—and a number of National Resource Centers, including the Center for Middle Eastern Studies. Chicago also operates or is affiliated with a number of research institutions apart from the university proper. The university partially manages Argonne National Laboratory, part of the United States Department of Energy's national laboratory system, and has a joint stake in Fermilab, a nearby particle physics laboratory, as well as a stake in the Apache Point Observatory in Sunspot, New Mexico. Faculty and students at the adjacent Toyota Technological Institute at Chicago collaborate with the university, In 2013, the university announced that it was affiliating the formerly independent Marine Biological Laboratory in Woods Hole, Mass. Although formally unrelated, the National Opinion Research Center is located on Chicago's campus.", 'question': 'Topic: University of Chicago\nHow many research centers does the university run on campus?', 'answer': '113'}, {'title': 'University of Chicago', 'context': "The university operates 12 research institutes and 113 research centers on campus. Among these are the Oriental Institute—a museum and research center for Near Eastern studies owned and operated by the university—and a number of National Resource Centers, including the Center for Middle Eastern Studies