09:06:11 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Victoria and Albert Museum\n1. The Victoria and Albert Museum showcases the work of not only British artists and craftspeople, but also European artists and imports from Asia.', "Victoria and Albert Museum\n2. The museum's collection includes work by renowned designers and artists such as Gian Lorenzo Bernini, Grinling Gibbons, Daniel Marot, Louis Laguerre, Antonio Verrio, Sir James Thornhill, William Kent, Robert Adam, Josiah Wedgwood, Matthew Boulton, Canova, Thomas Chippendale, Pugin, William Morris, and more.", 'Victoria and Albert Museum\n3. The museum represents the influence of patrons on the development of taste, including works from the collections of notable patrons such as Horace Walpole, William Thomas Beckford, and Thomas Hope.', "Victoria and Albert Museum\n4. The museum's collection spans various styles and periods, reflecting the diverse range of artistic and cultural influences on British design and craftsmanship.", 'Victoria and Albert Museum\n5. The Victoria and Albert Museum serves as a comprehensive resource for understanding the evolution of design and the impact of European and Asian influences on British art and culture.', 'Victoria and Albert Museum\nNot only the work of British artists and craftspeople is on display, but also work produced by European artists that was purchased or commissioned by British patrons, as well as imports from Asia, including porcelain, cloth and wallpaper. Designers and artists whose work is on display in the galleries include Gian Lorenzo Bernini, Grinling Gibbons, Daniel Marot, Louis Laguerre, Antonio Verrio, Sir James Thornhill, William Kent, Robert Adam, Josiah Wedgwood, Matthew Boulton, Canova, Thomas Chippendale, Pugin, William Morris. Patrons who have influenced taste are also represented by works of art from their collections, these include: Horace Walpole (a major influence on the Gothic Revival), William Thomas Beckford and Thomas Hope.'], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Victoria and Albert Museum', 'context': 'Not only the work of British artists and craftspeople is on display, but also work produced by European artists that was purchased or commissioned by British patrons, as well as imports from Asia, including porcelain, cloth and wallpaper. Designers and artists whose work is on display in the galleries include Gian Lorenzo Bernini, Grinling Gibbons, Daniel Marot, Louis Laguerre, Antonio Verrio, Sir James Thornhill, William Kent, Robert Adam, Josiah Wedgwood, Matthew Boulton, Canova, Thomas Chippendale, Pugin, William Morris. Patrons who have influenced taste are also represented by works of art from their collections, these include: Horace Walpole (a major influence on the Gothic Revival), William Thomas Beckford and Thomas Hope.', 'question': 'Topic: Victoria and Albert Museum\nWho purchased or commissioned the works of European artists included the British galleries of the V&A?', 'answer': 'British patrons'}, {'title': 'Victoria and Albert Museum', 'context': 'Not only the work of British artists and craftspeople is on display, but also work produced by European artists that was purchased or commissioned by British patrons, as well as imports from Asia, including porcelain, cloth and wallpaper. Designers and artists whose work is on display in the galleries include Gian Lorenzo Bernini, Grinling Gibbons, Daniel Marot, Louis Laguerre, Antonio Verrio, Sir James Thornhill, William Kent, Robert Adam, Josiah Wedgwood, Matthew Boulton, Canova, Thomas Chippendale, Pugin, William Morris. Patrons who have influenced taste are also represented by works of art from their collections, these include: Horace Walpole (a major influence on the Gothic Revival), William Thomas Beckford and Thomas Hope.', 'question': 'Topic: Victoria and Albert Museum\nSome non-British works in the British galleries were imported from which continent?', 'answer': 'Asia'}, {'title': 'Victoria and Albert Museum', 'context': 'Not only the work of British artists and craftspeople is on display, but also work produced by European artists that was purchased or commissioned by British patrons, as well as imports from Asia, including porcelain, cloth and wallpaper. Designers and artists whose work is on display in the galleries include Gian Lorenzo Bernini, Grinling Gibbons, Daniel Marot, Louis Laguerre, Antonio Verrio, Sir James Thornhill, William Kent, Robert Adam, Josiah Wedgwood, Matthew Boulton, Canova, Thomas Chippendale, Pugin, William Morris. Patrons who have influenced taste are also represented by works of art from their collections, these include: Horace Walpole (a major influence on the Gothic Revival), William Thomas Beckford and Thomas Hope.', 'question': "Topic: Victoria and Albert Museum\nWhich Italian that is credited with the creating the Baroque style of sculpture is represented in the V&A's British galleries?", 'answer': 'Gian Lorenzo Bernini'}, {'title': 'Victoria and Albert Museum', 'context': 'Not only the work of British artists and craftspeople is on display, but also work produced by European artists that was purchased or commissioned by British patrons, as well as imports from Asia, including porcelain, cloth and wallpaper. Designers and artists whose work is on display in the galleries include Gian Lorenzo Bernini, Grinling Gibbons, Daniel Marot, Louis Laguerre, Antonio Verrio, Sir James Thornhill, William Kent, Robert Adam, Josiah Wedgwood, Matthew Boulton, Canova, Thomas Chippendale, Pugin, William Morris. Patrons who have influenced taste are also represented by works of art from their collections, these include: Horace Walpole (a major influence on the Gothic Revival), William Thomas Beckford and Thomas Hope.', 'question': "Topic: Victoria and Albert Museum\nWhich artist who had a major influence on the Gothic Revival is represented in the V&A's British galleries?", 'answer': 'Horace Walpole'}, {'title': 'Victoria and Albert Museum', 'context': 'Not only the work of British artists and craftspeople is on display, but also work produced by European artists that was purchased or commissioned by British patrons, as well as imports from Asia, including porcelain, cloth and wallpaper. Designers and artists whose work is on display in the galleries include Gian Lorenzo Bernini, Grinling Gibbons, Daniel Marot, Louis Laguerre, Antonio Verrio, Sir James Thornhill, William Kent, Robert Adam, Josiah Wedgwood, Matthew Boulton, Canova, Thomas Chippendale, Pugin, William Morris. Patrons who have influenced taste are also represented by works of art from their collections, these include: Horace Walpole (a major influence on the Gothic Revival), William Thomas Beckford and Thomas Hope.', 'question': "Topic: Victoria and Albert Museum\nWhat type of works from Asia are included in the V&A's British galleries?", 'answer': 'porcelain, cloth and wallpaper'}], 'lora_rank': 32, 'lora_alpha': 64, 'lora_dropout': 0.0, 'finetune_epochs': 10, 'finetune_lr': 0.001, 'batch_size': 1, 'gradient_accumulation_steps': 1, 'end_mask_substring': ''}
