09:08:25 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Genghis Khan\n1. The Tanguts were not prepared for the attack and quickly fell to the Mongol forces.', "Genghis Khan\n2. Genghis Khan's quick victory suggests that his army was well-trained and strategic in their attacks.", "Genghis Khan\n3. The Tangut general's challenge to a battle near the Helan Mountains indicates a potential shift in strategy or a desire to test the Mongol army.", "Genghis Khan\n4. The Mongol's successful siege of Lingzhou and crossing of the Yellow River demonstrate their ability to overcome strategic challenges and adapt to new terrains.", "Genghis Khan\n5. The defeat of the Tangut relief army further showcases the Mongol's military prowess and ability to outmaneuver their opponents.", 'Genghis Khan\n6. The omen seen by Genghis Khan during his campaign adds a layer of mystique and suggests a belief in divine favor or guidance.', 'Genghis Khan\n7. The passage implies that the Tanguts were not able to effectively defend against the Mongol invasion, ultimately leading to their downfall.', "Genghis Khan\n8. Genghis Khan's success in this campaign may have solidified his power and reputation as a skilled and feared military leader.", 'Genghis Khan\n9. The rapid succession of victories suggests that the Mongols were well-prepared and had a clear plan of attack.', "Genghis Khan\n10. The Tangut's inability to resist the Mongol forces may indicate a weakness or vulnerability within their own military or political structure.", 'Genghis Khan\nIn 1226, immediately after returning from the west, Genghis Khan began a retaliatory attack on the Tanguts. His armies quickly took Heisui, Ganzhou, and Suzhou (not the Suzhou in Jiangsu province), and in the autumn he took Xiliang-fu[disambiguation needed]. One of the Tangut generals challenged the Mongols to a battle near Helan Mountains but was defeated. In November, Genghis laid siege to the Tangut city Lingzhou and crossed the Yellow River, defeating the Tangut relief army. According to legend, it was here that Genghis Khan reportedly saw a line of five stars arranged in the sky and interpreted it as an omen of his victory.'], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Genghis Khan', 'context': 'In 1226, immediately after returning from the west, Genghis Khan began a retaliatory attack on the Tanguts. His armies quickly took Heisui, Ganzhou, and Suzhou (not the Suzhou in Jiangsu province), and in the autumn he took Xiliang-fu[disambiguation needed]. One of the Tangut generals challenged the Mongols to a battle near Helan Mountains but was defeated. In November, Genghis laid siege to the Tangut city Lingzhou and crossed the Yellow River, defeating the Tangut relief army. According to legend, it was here that Genghis Khan reportedly saw a line of five stars arranged in the sky and interpreted it as an omen of his victory.', 'question': 'Topic: Genghis Khan\nIn which year did Genghis Khan strike against the Tanguts?', 'answer': '1226'}, {'title': 'Genghis Khan', 'context': 'In 1226, immediately after returning from the west, Genghis Khan began a retaliatory attack on the Tanguts. His armies quickly took Heisui, Ganzhou, and Suzhou (not the Suzhou in Jiangsu province), and in the autumn he took Xiliang-fu[disambiguation needed]. One of the Tangut generals challenged the Mongols to a battle near Helan Mountains but was defeated. In November, Genghis laid siege to the Tangut city Lingzhou and crossed the Yellow River, defeating the Tangut relief army. According to legend, it was here that Genghis Khan reportedly saw a line of five stars arranged in the sky and interpreted it as an omen of his victory.', 'question': 'Topic: Genghis Khan\nWhat season was it when Genghis Khan took Xiliang-fu from the Tanguts?', 'answer': 'autumn'}, {'title': 'Genghis Khan', 'context': 'In 1226, immediately after returning from the west, Genghis Khan began a retaliatory attack on the Tanguts. His armies quickly took Heisui, Ganzhou, and Suzhou (not the Suzhou in Jiangsu province), and in the autumn he took Xiliang-fu[disambiguation needed]. One of the Tangut generals challenged the Mongols to a battle near Helan Mountains but was defeated. In November, Genghis laid siege to the Tangut city Lingzhou and crossed the Yellow River, defeating the Tangut relief army. According to legend, it was here that Genghis Khan reportedly saw a line of five stars arranged in the sky and interpreted it as an omen of his victory.', 'question': 'Topic: Genghis Khan\nWho won the battle near the Helan mountains?', 'answer': 'the Mongols'}, {'title': 'Genghis Khan', 'context': 'In 1226, immediately after returning from the west, Genghis Khan began a retaliatory attack on the Tanguts. His armies quickly took Heisui, Ganzhou, and Suzhou (not the Suzhou in Jiangsu province), and in the autumn he took Xiliang-fu[disambiguation needed]. One of the Tangut generals challenged the Mongols to a battle near Helan Mountains but was defeated. In November, Genghis laid siege to the Tangut city Lingzhou and crossed the Yellow River, defeating the Tangut relief army. According to legend, it was here that Genghis Khan reportedly saw a line of five stars arranged in the sky and interpreted it as an omen of his victory.', 'question': 'Topic: Genghis Khan\nWhat river did Genghis Khan cross before defeating the main Tangut army?', 'answer': 'the Yellow River'}, {'title': 'Genghis Khan', 'context': 'In 1226, immediately after returning from the west, Genghis Khan began a retaliatory attack on the Tanguts. His armies quickly took Heisui, Ganzhou, and Suzhou (not the Suzhou in Jiangsu province), and in the autumn he took Xiliang-fu[disambiguation needed]. One of the Tangut generals challenged the Mongols to a battle near Helan Mountains but was defeated. In November, Genghis laid siege to the Tangut city Lingzhou and crossed the Yellow River, defeating the Tangut relief army. According to legend, it was here that Genghis Khan reportedly saw a line of five stars arranged in the sky and interpreted it as an omen of his victory.', 'question': 'Topic: Genghis Khan\nWhat omen was Genghis Khan reported to have seen assuring his coming victory against the Tanguts?', 'answer': 'a line of five stars arranged in the sky'}], 'lora_rank': 32, 'lora_alpha': 64, 'lora_dropout': 0.0, 'finetune_epochs': 10, 'finetune_lr': 0.001, 'batch_size': 1, 'gradient_accumulation_steps': 1, 'end_mask_substring': ''}
