: 'Teacher', 'context': 'In Tibetan Buddhism the teachers of Dharma in Tibet are most commonly called a Lama. A Lama who has through phowa and siddhi consciously determined to be reborn, often many times, in order to continue their Bodhisattva vow is called a Tulku.', 'question': 'Topic: Teacher\nWhat has a Lama determined to do?', 'answer': 'be reborn'}, {'title': 'Teacher', 'context': 'In Tibetan Buddhism the teachers of Dharma in Tibet are most commonly called a Lama. A Lama who has through phowa and siddhi consciously determined to be reborn, often many times, in order to continue their Bodhisattva vow is called a Tulku.', 'question': 'Topic: Teacher\nWhat is the name of a Bodhisattva vow?', 'answer': 'Tulku'}, {'title': 'Teacher', 'context': 'In Tibetan Buddhism the teachers of Dharma in Tibet are most commonly called a Lama. A Lama who has through phowa and siddhi consciously determined to be reborn, often many times, in order to continue their Bodhisattva vow is called a Tulku.', 'question': 'Topic: Teacher\nHow much has a Lama agreed to be reborn?', 'answer': 'often many times'}, {'title': 'Teacher', 'context': 'In Tibetan Buddhism the teachers of Dharma in Tibet are most commonly called a Lama. A Lama who has through phowa and siddhi consciously determined to be reborn, often many times, in order to continue their Bodhisattva vow is called a Tulku.', 'question': 'Topic: Teacher\nWhat helped the Lama determine to be reborn?', 'answer': 'through phowa and siddhi'}], 'lora_rank': 32, 'lora_alpha': 64, 'lora_dropout': 0.0, 'finetune_epochs': 10, 'finetune_lr': 0.001, 'batch_size': 1, 'gradient_accumulation_steps': 1, 'end_mask_substring': ''}
